{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra","id":1440513,"title":"Reality Zones and the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-18T17:17:13-07:00","id":1440513,"title":"Reality Zones and the Umbra","content":"This was inspired by a discussion in a recent thread about \u201cThe Technocracy and Star Trek\u201d, which veered into discussing Disembodiment/Void Adaptation and how \u201cprimal mages like Dreamspeakers and Verbenae\u201d got to hang around in the Umbra much longer than anyone else before Disembodiment set in. I expressed an issue with \u201cprimal mages\u201d getting that sorry of an edge without any drawbacks, and was challenged on it. With that in mind:<br /> <br /> Actually, my problem isn't with primal mages having a free advantage in the Umbra. I mean, I do have something of a problem with that; but it's not my main problem. My main problem is with there being <i>an</i> Umbra, singular, with a consistent set of rules that applies across the board. I could see the idea of the \u201cmiddle Umbra\u201d being a sort of home turf for mages who have an animistic or back-to-nature bent to their Focus, and thus being able to hang out there for long stretches of time without any fear of Disembodiment. But should the Astral and Dark Umbrae be as accommodating to them? Shouldn't other kinds of Foci, such as the ones supported by Hermetics and Euthanatoi respectively, get that benefit in the Upper and Lower Umbrae? And then there's the matter of Etherspace: shouldn't the likes of the Sons of Ether be the ones who have no problem staying there for long stretches of time, rather than shamans and witches? <br /> <br /> The idea that it's always the witches and shamans who get this benefit no matter what the environment is like? That's the real issue. <br /> <br /> And related to that is the notion that all magic is coincidental in the Umbra. Again, this is a case of treating everything with the word \u201cUmbra\u201d in it as a monolithic block, when clearly different parts of the Umbra have their own characteristics; and it isn't until you get out into the Deep Umbra that the character of the environment is that it is undefined. <br /> <br /> Still, I'm not one to completely throw out what's come before; I'm more inclined to rework it into something that hews as closely to the original as possible while making more sense to me. So let me propose this: there <i>is</i> a universal characteristic that holds throughout the Umbrae that distinguishes them from Earth. But it isn't that all Magick is Coincidental; it's that <i>there are no Earthly Foundations</i>. <br /> <br /> In this take on the Umbrae, there Reality Zones in the Umbra as well as on Earth. Without a human presence or Earthly Foundations, they can be much more fluid than their Earth-bound counterparts (easier to change, and less restricted in how they can change) and much more permissive (on average, fewer things are Vulgar in an Umbral Reality Zone than in an Earthside one); but they're there. If your Focus is one that's largely aligned with the Umbral Reality Zone you happen to find yourself in, then you don't have to worry so much about Disembodiment; and of course, you also needn't worry so much about Vulgar Magick, as your Magick is almost certainly not Vulgar. <br /> <br /> The only place that doesn't have Reality Zones is the Deep Umbra. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T19:19:38-07:00","id":1440531,"title":"","content":"I'm coming at least partly from a Werewolf cosmology/unified WoD perspective, once firmly centered on Earth, and I admittedly have a hard time understanding consensual reality. I admit that I am totally biased against the Technocrats. So this may or may not make sense to anyone who had the good fortune to be able to play Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> The way I see it, the Technocratic paradigm is a lie and always has been. Not because their technology is a lie, but because they lie about everything else not existing. So Paradox does what it does <b>now</b> because the Technocrats have utterly screwed up the sleeper consensus with their lies. In the Umbra, reality is still what it always was: fluid, magical, alive, and spiritual. It's muted and weakened and sickly compared to what it was millennia ago, maybe due to the stupidly thick Gauntlet, but it's still fundamentally spiritual. There are no ignorant humans out there to lie to about the way reality works, and spirits can get in your face and remind you that they do exist. It's my understanding that in the distant past, when the Gauntlet was a lot thinner and quintessence/vis/gnosis/glamour was a lot more plentiful, there wasn't really Paradox in the material world - that the Scourge started some time in the Dark Ages or Sorcerer's Crusade time as a result of the growing dominance of Christianity, but it didn't exist before that.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how the growing Banality of humanity has slowly strangled a lot of the glamour out of the Autumn world, but the Dreaming is still made of glamour. The spirit worlds <b>are</b> magic and spirit, that's what they're made of. They can't be forced to deny themselves. Not even in the Abyss. Even the Gauntlet and the Shroud are ultimately unnatural - they were violations inflicted upon a cosmos that was once whole, and wholly spiritual.<br /> <br /> What do exist are the rules or laws of each Realm. Don't try healing magick in Malfeas if you don't love cancer. Don't try to create permanent static magic in the Radiance. Don't try to set things on fire underwater in Umi, the Dragon Kingdom of the Sea. Don't do things against the rules in the Grand Hall, even if you don't know the rules. Don't try to use your fancy computer in Pangaea. Don't try to create a big light source down in the Abyss. Don't do... something in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> There are also things that become the equivalent of chaos magick. Like Entropy in the Underworld, or explosions in the Shade Realm of Forces, or sensory deprivation meditations in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> But denial? No, I don't think flat denial about the spiritual truth about reality and magic's existence is possible in any place that hasn't been cut off from the spirit worlds by the Gauntlet and Shroud, and splattered with centuries of Technocratic propaganda, especially in the fluid &quot;space&quot; between Realms. Probably in Dystopia and the Scar, magick does best to be flavored towards technomagic, but it still doesn't have to obey the artificially narrow rules of Technocratic consensus technology. I think that only in places utterly under the control of Control would the Technocratic paradigm actually replace the true, magical nature of reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like your idea that Verbenae are protected from disconnection only in the Middle Umbra, and other mysticks would have an easier time in some other Umbra instead, depending on their paradigm (or whatever it's called in M20). So Hermetics and Singers and Cultists and Akashics in the High Umbra, Euthanatoi in the Underworld, Etherites in Etherspace, Virtual Adepts in the Digital Web of course, Dreamspeakers in whichever Umbra is home to whatever spirit(s) they're closest to. Kinfolk are safe in the Middle Umbra, and maybe Kinain are in the Dreaming (but the Dreaming has its own rules I guess). Anyone with the advantage of a familiar or a totem or a merit is golden. That said, I think any Spirit-using paradigm should be equally OK in the Deep Umbra. And I personally think that disconnection should be faster in the Realms of Mind and Spirit, and never happen to anyone in the Realms of Matter and Life.<br /> <br /> But of your idea seems to raise a problem: if someone is protected in whatever part of the Umbra is most in tune with their paradigm, the Horizon Realms should be one of the last places that a mage disconnects (if they're in their group's Realm).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But the reason I challenged you was my question about game balance: is it a bad thing if mysticks get some unique advantages? Aren't Technocrats automatically <i>strongly</i> advantaged by the setting? They sure look like they are, but I'm asking if my impression is correct. I tend to root for underdogs and dangit, the Technos are the ones who created the Avatar Storm. On purpose! So part of me just says they deserve to get burned by it, more than other mages. Not that there is anything resembling cosmic justice or fair karma in the WoD. But, er, I am in favor of game balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-18-2021, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T20:50:00-07:00","id":1440534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440531#post1440531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm coming at least partly from a Werewolf cosmology/unified WoD perspective, once firmly centered on Earth, and I admittedly have a hard time understanding consensual reality. So this may or may not make sense to anyone who had the good fortune to be able to play Mage.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, the Technocratic paradigm is a lie and always has been. Not because their technology is a lie, but because they lie about everything else not existing. So Paradox does what it does <b>now</b> because the Technocrats have utterly screwed up the sleeper consensus with their lies. In the Umbra, reality is still what it always was: fluid, magical, alive, and spiritual. It's muted and weakened and sickly compared to what it was millennia ago, maybe due to the stupidly thick Gauntlet, but it's still fundamentally spiritual. There are no ignorant humans out there to lie to about the way reality works, and spirits can get in your face and remind you that they do exist. It's my understanding that in the distant past, when the Gauntlet was a lot thinner and quintessence/vis/gnosis/glamour was a lot more plentiful, there wasn't really Paradox in the material world - that the Scourge started some time in the Dark Ages or Sorcerer's Crusade time as a result of the growing dominance of Christianity, but it didn't exist before that.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how the growing Banality of humanity has slowly strangled the glamour out of the Autumn world, but the Dreaming is still made of glamour. The spirit worlds <b>are</b> magic and spirit, that's what they're made of. They can't be forced to deny themselves. Not even in the Abyss. Even the material world, the Gauntlet, and the Shroud are ultimately unnatural - they were violations inflicted upon a cosmos that was once whole, and wholly spiritual.<br /> <br /> What do exist are the rules or laws of each Realm. Don't try healing magick in Malfeas if you don't like cancer. Don't try to create permanent static magic in the Radiance. Don't try to set things on fire underwater in Umi, the Dragon Kingdom of the Sea. Don't do things against the rules in the Grand Hall, even if you don't know the rules. Don't try to use your fancy computer in Pangaea. Don't try to create a big light source down in the Abyss. Don't do... something in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> There are also things that become the equivalent of chaos magick. Like Entropy in the Underworld, or explosions in the Shade Realm of Forces, or sensory deprivation meditations in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> But denial? No, I don't think flat denial about the spiritual truth about reality and magic's existence is possible in any place that hasn't been cut off from the spirit worlds by the Gauntlet and Shroud, and splattered with centuries of Technocratic propaganda. Maybe in Dystopia and the Scar, magick does best to be flavored towards technomagic, but it still doesn't have to obey they artificially narrow rules of Technocratic pseudoscience. I think that only in places utterly under the control of Control would the Technocratic paradigm actually replace the true, fluid nature of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could definitely see many Dreamspeakers thinking this way; it's a very Spirit-centric view of things, where spirits and spirituality are the ultimate truths and everything else is judged against them. I wouldn't present it as <i>the</i> ultimate Truth, for the same reason why <b>Mage</b> hasn't described the Technocracy as pawns of the Weaver in <i>ages</i>; the idea that technology is of the Weaver is a <b>Werewolf</b>ism, and not something that <b>Mage</b> takes as an absolute: in <b>Mage</b> terms, it's what the Garou believe; but that doesn't make it true. Heck, <b>Mage</b> has long since moved past the idea that the Weaver <i>is</i> Stasis; in <b>Mage</b>, Stasis may very well be more fundamental than the Weaver is. And Technocrats aren't even beholden to Stasis these days; the few references to them being devoted to it are holdovers from the earliest edition of the game, and great efforts have been made to downplay and reinterpret them in less of a \u201cpawns of the Weaver\u201d approach. Which doesn't keep the Garou from thinking that they're pawns of the Weaver; but <b>Werewolf</b> doesn't determine what's true in <b>Mage</b>. <br /> <br /> As well, Technocratic Reality Zones make a <i>lot</i> of things Vulgar \u2014 as do most other Reality Zones. It's just the way of things: to believe that some things are possible, you almost <i>have to</i> believe that other things aren't. (There are some exceptions to this, such as the eternal mission of the Etherites to gradually expand the bounds of what's accepted as possible until nothing is left out; but that's more aspirational than something that anyone has actually accomplished). But with that said, Paradox isn't a human creation: per the Earthly Foundations, there are certain things that tend to cause Paradox even if the locals sincerely believe in them. And among the examples given of Earthly Foundations is crossing the Gauntlet. The Union has sought to <i>strengthen</i> the Gauntlet; but it didn't <i>create</i> it; as far as anyone knows, the Gauntlet has always existed. Paradox has been called other things over the centuries: the Straits in Victorian times, the Scourge during the Sorcerers Crusade, Backlash in the Dark Ages; but it's always been there for as long as there have been mages. And no, it <i>wasn't</i> created by Christianity: <i>Ars Magica</i> has something in it about the Divine Realm of Power interfering with the Magical, Faerie, and Infernal Realms of Power; but that's not something that was ever ported over to the World of Darkness, beyond perhaps the powers of True Faith. And even that isn't a Christianity-only thing: True Faith has been around as long as there have been people who believe in something greater than themselves. Certainly, it's not responsible for Paradox. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440531#post1440531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your idea that Verbenae (and Kinfolk?) are protected from disconnection only in the Middle Umbra, and other mysticks would have an easier time in some other Umbra instead, depending on their paradigm (or whatever it's called in M20). So Hermetics and Singers and Cultists and Akashics in the High Umbra, Euthanatoi in the Underworld, Etherites in Etherspace, Virtual Adepts in the Digital Web of course, Dreamspeakers in whichever Umbra is home to whatever spirit(s) they're closest to, and maybe Kinain in the Dreaming. Unless they have the advantage of a familiar or a totem or a merit, in which case they're golden. That said, I think any spirit-using paradigm should be equally OK in the Deep Umbra. And I personally think that disconnection should be faster in the Realms of Mind and Spirit, and never happen to anyone in the Realms of Matter and Life.</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, there are many who would argue that the Digital Web isn't a spirit world. One of the points that supports this is that Disembodiment simply isn't a thing in the Digital Web. As well, when the Avatar Storm struck, it did nothing to interfere with access to the Digital Web. There may be, and in fact probably are, other \u201cotherworlds\u201d that aren't spiritual in nature, either; a case could be made that the Dreaming isn't, for example. <br /> <br /> More generally, the whole idea that everything otherworldly centers around the Umbra is another <b>Werewolf</b>ism. The Virtual Adepts, for example, view the Tapestry through the notion of the Hypersphere, where the Correspondence Point is at the center of everything; the physical world and most of the otherworlds (including the Umbrae) exist on the \u201csurface\u201d of the Hypersphere; and Virtual Space (which includes the Digital Web) is what connects the Correspondence Point to the rest of the Tapestry. The Alder Bole, which spiritualists say is the center of reality, is viewed by the Virtual Adepts as merely the spirit world's representation of the Correspondence Point. I'm not saying they're right; but I wouldn't say that they're wrong, either. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440531#post1440531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But of your idea seems to raise a problem: if someone is protected in whatever part of the Umbra is most in tune with their paradigm, the Horizon Realms should be one of the last places that a mage disconnects (if they're in their Tradition's realm).</div> </div> </div> </div> Normally, that would be true. But the Avatar Storm screwed things up; and for its duration, <i>nobody</i> got more than three months <i>anywhere</i> in the Umbra before they Disembodied. <br /> <br /> I'll address the rest in the original thread, because it doesn't really have anything to do with this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T21:11:58-07:00","id":1440538,"title":"","content":"On principle regarding Reality Zones/Paradigms onto an Umbral Realm? Yes. <br /> <br /> There is definitely a limit to how much you can get away with Effects and just claiming they\u2019re all Coincidental \u2018cause Umbra realm. <br /> <br /> We technically already have a precedent with the Digital Web in that if you explicitly try to pull any Effects from a mystical Paradigm are immediately considered Vulgar. <br /> <br /> Or to be more direct: yeah I would think trying to create a permanent, ever-cold glacier in the Realm of Fire would be Vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T21:20:01-07:00","id":1440539,"title":"","content":"I think the reasons they made Technocrats disadvantaged in terms of Umbral survival are mainly practical: if Technocrats were not so disadvantaged, wouldn't they just build a massive empire in the Umbra? Dreamspeakers and Verbena aren't going to do that. It simply isn't in their nature, nor their numbers. But the Technocracy?<br /> <br /> Same reason they created the storm: to keep earth important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T21:24:24-07:00","id":1440540,"title":"","content":"Two points: first, the malleability of Umbral Reality makes it hard to <i>keep</i> an advantage there; easy come, easy go. Second, the Technocracy didn't create the Avatar Storm; at least, not deliberately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T21:30:40-07:00","id":1440541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440538#post1440538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We technically already have a precedent with the Digital Web in that if you explicitly try to pull any Effects from a mystical Paradigm are immediately considered Vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor point of order: by default, the Digital Web doesn't prohibit mystick praxis itself, but rather, all effects require a visible and readily discernible source. A Hermetic shooting a fireball from a magic wand would actually have an easier time than a Black Suit attempting to mind controlled people with rhetoric alone. Granted, technomancers generally run into this issue less than mysticks, but that's not technically where the divide lies.<br /> <br /> This doesn't hold true everywhere, of course. Zones can be formatted by just about anybody with the knowhow to operate on whatever &quot;Consensus&quot; the creator wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T23:32:44-07:00","id":1440548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440534#post1440534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, there are many who would argue that the Digital Web isn't a spirit world. One of the points that supports this is that Disembodiment simply isn't a thing in the Digital Web.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welllllll....<br /> The problem with the Digital Web there could be something as humble as a lack of observed data in that regard.<br /> Unlike most ways of traveling to the Umbra, the Digital Web is more or less majorly traversed by ways of sending your mind there while the body remains in normal meatspace. So not only is the way of traveling there quite different, (which miiiiight account for a lack of Avatar Storm mechanics), but also it might account for most Mages involved with the digital web simply *thinking* that disembodiement is not a thing over there - after all it is hardly possible to spend more than a few *days* there by most means of DIgital Web travel without starting to run into serious health problems in meatspace. Not even speaking of, uh, hygiene problems that take a way shorter amount of time.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: The ways to run into the problem of possible disembodiement on the DIgital Web are severely limited or impossible in the vast majority of ways of normally accessing it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T04:33:07-07:00","id":1440576,"title":"","content":"(Heh; Ambrosia said that there's a lack of <i>data</i> regarding the Digital Web\u2026)<br /> <br /> The rules for access to the DW allow for three levels of access: sensory visitation (which doesn't require any Magick at all), Astral Immersion (Corr/Data 2), and Holistic Immersion (Life 4, Forces 2, Corr/Data 2). That last one is roughly analogous to Stepping Sideways in that you fully enter the DW and interact with it as if you were physically in an otherworld; but it's described more like a transformation of a Life Pattern into a digital pattern. Holistic Immersion is only \u201crare\u201d to the extent that VAs with Life 4, Corr/Data 2, Forces 2 are rare; Life isn't a Sphere that one typically finds in a VA arsenal. But it's common enough that there isn't a shortage of VAs who do the Tron thing of digitizing themselves to visit their Reality 2.0 in person. <br /> <br /> In essence, it would be like the rules insisting that one must transform into a spirit in order to physically enter the Umbra. So Disembodiment isn't an issue in the DW because you're <i>already</i> \u201cdisembodied\u201d when you arrive. Except that you don't suffer any ill effects from it and can easily reverse the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-10-2022, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T07:55:30-07:00","id":1440598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440576#post1440576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In essence, it would be like the rules insisting that one must transform into a spirit in order to physically enter the Umbra. So Disembodiment isn't an issue in the DW because you're <i>already</i> \u201cdisembodied\u201d when you arrive. Except that you don't suffer any ill effects from it and can easily reverse the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, true, I guess there is a certain share of holistic immersers...the question is if, of the share that *do* this, any noticable amount actually do it for months at at time.<br /> <br /> But *if* some do and it works well without losing oneself ( ...or are those that are staying there for JUUUUUST a bit longer already disembodied without noticing...? Fragementation is a bitch... ), then the reverse approach might be true - a voluntary and controlled turning into Ephemera when traditionally sidestepping might avoid disembodiement the same way.<br /> This calls for...<br /> <br /> SCIENCE! (And alternative mystical experimentations akin to such things)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-19-2021, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T08:25:04-07:00","id":1440600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440598#post1440598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, true, I guess there is a certain share of holistic immersers...the question is if, of the share that *do* this, any noticable amount actually do it for months at at time.</div> </div> </div> </div>DW2.0 had something in it about how there had one been holistic immersers who had basically immigrated to the DW; but then the White Out happened, and everyone found out why it's not yet a good idea to do that.<br /> <br /> In short, the problem isn't Disembodiment; it's that Reality 2.0 isn't stable enough yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440598#post1440598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But *if* some do and it works well without losing oneself ( ...or are those that are staying there for JUUUUUST a bit longer already disembodied without noticing...? Fragementation is a bitch... ), then the reverse approach might be true - a voluntary and controlled turning into Ephemera when traditionally sidestepping might avoid disembodiement the same way.<br /> This calls for...<br /> <br /> SCIENCE! (And alternative mystical experimentations akin to such things)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only true if the situations are analogous. My point is that it appears that the similarities between them are only surface deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T10:18:45-07:00","id":1440612,"title":"","content":"Edit: See, my difficulty with Mage consensus cosmology is that it seems to say nothing is true, or everything is equally true. Then we can't say anything definitive about anything. But yet there have to be definite game rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440534#post1440534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could definitely see many Dreamspeakers thinking this way; it's a very Spirit-centric view of things, where spirits and spirituality are the ultimate truths and everything else is judged against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirit worlds collectively are a heck of a lot larger and deeper than the material worlds, so it's hard to argue that the material world is more fundamental. Being a place of spirit-less matter, the material world is the odd duck out. Or the material world and the Shade Realm of Matter. Assuming the former isn't somewhere inside the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440534#post1440534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't present it as <i>the</i> ultimate Truth, for the same reason why <b>Mage</b> hasn't described the Technocracy as pawns of the Weaver in <i>ages</i>; the idea that technology is of the Weaver is a <b>Werewolf</b>ism, and not something that <b>Mage</b> takes as an absolute: in <b>Mage</b> terms, it's what the Garou believe; but that doesn't make it true. Heck, <b>Mage</b> has long since moved past the idea that the Weaver <i>is</i> Stasis; in <b>Mage</b>, Stasis may very well be more fundamental than the Weaver is. And Technocrats aren't even beholden to Stasis these days; the few references to them being devoted to it are holdovers from the earliest edition of the game, and great efforts have been made to downplay and reinterpret them in less of a \u201cpawns of the Weaver\u201d approach. Which doesn't keep the Garou from thinking that they're pawns of the Weaver; but <b>Werewolf</b> doesn't determine what's true in <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The science+technology = Bad concept wasn't a good design choice for either game, really. I have a friend who loves the CofD but can't stand the cWoD because of it, and I can't really blame her.<br /> <br /> But the Technocracy are also all about control, about limiting possibilities and options, about censoring knowledge as a weapon to remove things from reality, and about explaining everything in reductionistic ways that eliminate spirituality, souls, intuition, and lots of other details that they know do actually exist. Those goals are also Stasis. (In Werewolf terms, Stasis and the Weaver would be the same thing. By definition, nothing but the Almighty Creator can be bigger than the Weaver because it's inherently 1/3 of all reality.) If Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy are each 1/3 of reality in Mage, then the same is true: you can't have something bigger than Stasis, except for God/the One.<br /> <br /> Edit: And how can the things Technocrats tell the 'Masses' not be lies? They say magic is impossible, that &quot;reality deviants&quot; and spirits don't exist, but they know all three are real and do exist. They insist there is no spirit world, but they know it exists and how to enter it. They censor scientific discoveries that they don't like.<br /> <br /> I wasn't saying the Technocrats created the Gauntlet or Shroud, of course. They appear to be making the Gauntlet thicker, but both barriers would have been created in prehistoric times, like the Stone Age or even earlier. Wraith seems to say the Shroud was created by the fear of death. Werewolf says the Gauntlet was created by the Weaver. In a unified WoD, <b>or</b> in Mage, humans couldn't know because they have no recorded history (oral or written) old enough to tell them anything about that time period. No Mage craft or Tradition is that old, so how would they know what happened then? Let alone claiming to know how the universe was created - humans didn't exist then so how would they know? Some spirits could know, but most mages don't talk to spirits, and some spirits could be lying. And if a spirit says &quot;this god created XYZ&quot; to an atheist mage, the mage'll just ignore what it said.<br /> <br /> You mentioned Earthly Foundations several times. Is this some term from the Technocratic paradigm, or an OOC game term? I have the same question about &quot;Reality Zone&quot;, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440534#post1440534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, Technocratic Reality Zones make a <i>lot</i> of things Vulgar \u2014 as do most other Reality Zones. It's just the way of things: to believe that some things are possible, you almost <i>have to</i> believe that other things aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree, at least not in an absolute sense. Maybe in Mage that is the case, but in terms of worldbuilding a plausible fantasy setting it isn't necessarily true. Some magic may require a higher level spell but that isn't the same as being absolutely impossible to do. It's possible to invent an internally-consistent fantasy magic system in which absolutely anything can be accomplished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440534#post1440534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox has been called other things over the centuries: the Straits in Victorian times, the Scourge during the Sorcerers Crusade, Backlash in the Dark Ages; but it's always been there for as long as there have been mages. And no, it <i>wasn't</i> created by Christianity: <i>Ars Magica</i> has something in it about the Divine Realm of Power interfering with the Magical, Faerie, and Infernal Realms of Power; but that's not something that was ever ported over to the World of Darkness, beyond perhaps the powers of True Faith. And even that isn't a Christianity-only thing: True Faith has been around as long as there have been people who believe in something greater than themselves. Certainly, it's not responsible for Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for clearing up my misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440534#post1440534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, there are many who would argue that the Digital Web isn't a spirit world. One of the points that supports this is that Disembodiment simply isn't a thing in the Digital Web. As well, when the Avatar Storm struck, it did nothing to interfere with access to the Digital Web. There may be, and in fact probably are, other \u201cotherworlds\u201d that aren't spiritual in nature, either; a case could be made that the Dreaming isn't, for example.<br /> <br /> More generally, the whole idea that everything otherworldly centers around the Umbra is another <b>Werewolf</b>ism. The Virtual Adepts, for example, view the Tapestry through the notion of the Hypersphere, where the Correspondence Point is at the center of everything; the physical world and most of the otherworlds (including the Umbrae) exist on the \u201csurface\u201d of the Hypersphere; and Virtual Space (which includes the Digital Web) is what connects the Correspondence Point to the rest of the Tapestry. The Alder Bole, which spiritualists say is the center of reality, is viewed by the Virtual Adepts as merely the spirit world's representation of the Correspondence Point. I'm not saying they're right; but I wouldn't say that they're wrong, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Virtual Adept paradigm is one I've never been able to understand. The Virtual Space has to predate computers to be the center of the universe. But if it isn't made of data and websites, what is it? I guess it must be made of thoughts, if it used to be the Qutb network. But in that case how is it different from the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-19-2021, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T10:36:13-07:00","id":1440615,"title":"","content":"Depending on VA in question, the correspondence point isn't even a *real* thing so much as a mathematical model of a specialized point that has a near zero distance from every possible point. It's more of a mathematical model or thought experiment. You don't have to view the VA world view as something only possible with computers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-19-2021, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T12:15:39-07:00","id":1440620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: See, my difficulty with Mage consensus cosmology is that it seems to say nothing is true, or everything is equally true. Then we can't say anything definitive about anything. But yet there have to be definite game rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because WoD cosmology is a mess and doesn't make sense if you try to line up all of the gameline's cosmologies together, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:15:15-07:00","id":1440626,"title":"","content":"I'll get back to Erinys' post later, when I have more time. But for the time being, what tasti man LH said. In fact, <b>Ascension</b> addresses this directly with its Fractured Cosmos theory, which posits the idea that there isn't a single World of Darkness but several of them that exist in parallel and resonate with each other. In essence, one per gameline. In the Werewolf cosmos, the Triat is indeed supreme as the Garou imagine them to be; but in the Vampire cosmos, you don't even have Garou, let alone the Triat; you have \u201clupines\u201d. And so on. It's basically the watsonian version of \u201cthe World of Darkness is whatever your Storyteller says that it is\u201d. <br /> <br /> And in true Mage tradition, it's not presented as an absolute Truth either. Just a theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T17:00:24-07:00","id":1440660,"title":"","content":"\u201c There is a theory which states that if ever anyone discovers exactly what the Universe is for and why it is here, it will instantly disappear and be replaced by something even more bizarre and inexplicable. <br /> <br /> There is another theory which states that this has already happened.\u201d<br /> <br /> -Douglas Adams","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T18:53:55-07:00","id":1440670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: See, my difficulty with Mage consensus cosmology is that it seems to say nothing is true, or everything is equally true. Then we can't say anything definitive about anything. But yet there have to be definite game rules.<br /> <br /> The spirit worlds collectively are a heck of a lot larger and deeper than the material worlds, so it's hard to argue that the material world is more fundamental. Being a place of spirit-less matter, the material world is the odd duck out. Or the material world and the Shade Realm of Matter. Assuming the former isn't somewhere inside the latter.<br /> <br /> The science+technology = Bad concept wasn't a good design choice for either game, really. I have a friend who loves the CofD but can't stand the cWoD because of it, and I can't really blame her.<br /> <br /> But the Technocracy are also all about control, about limiting possibilities and options, about censoring knowledge as a weapon to remove things from reality, and about explaining everything in reductionistic ways that eliminate spirituality, souls, intuition, and lots of other details that they know do actually exist. Those goals are also Stasis. (In Werewolf terms, Stasis and the Weaver would be the same thing. By definition, nothing but the Almighty Creator can be bigger than the Weaver because it's inherently 1/3 of all reality.) If Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy are each 1/3 of reality in Mage, then the same is true: you can't have something bigger than Stasis, except for God/the One.<br /> <br /> Edit: And how can the things Technocrats tell the 'Masses' not be lies? They say magic is impossible, that &quot;reality deviants&quot; and spirits don't exist, but they know all three are real and do exist. They insist there is no spirit world, but they know it exists and how to enter it. They censor scientific discoveries that they don't like.<br /> <br /> I wasn't saying the Technocrats created the Gauntlet or Shroud, of course. They appear to be making the Gauntlet thicker, but both barriers would have been created in prehistoric times, like the Stone Age or even earlier. Wraith seems to say the Shroud was created by the fear of death. Werewolf says the Gauntlet was created by the Weaver. In a unified WoD, <b>or</b> in Mage, humans couldn't know because they have no recorded history (oral or written) old enough to tell them anything about that time period. No Mage craft or Tradition is that old, so how would they know what happened then? Let alone claiming to know how the universe was created - humans didn't exist then so how would they know? Some spirits could know, but most mages don't talk to spirits, and some spirits could be lying. And if a spirit says &quot;this god created XYZ&quot; to an atheist mage, the mage'll just ignore what it said.<br /> <br /> You mentioned Earthly Foundations several times. Is this some term from the Technocratic paradigm, or an OOC game term? I have the same question about &quot;Reality Zone&quot;, too.<br /> <br /> I don't agree, at least not in an absolute sense. Maybe in Mage that is the case, but in terms of worldbuilding a plausible fantasy setting it isn't necessarily true. Some magic may require a higher level spell but that isn't the same as being absolutely impossible to do. It's possible to invent an internally-consistent fantasy magic system in which absolutely anything can be accomplished.<br /> <br /> Thank you for clearing up my misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adept paradigm is one I've never been able to understand. The Virtual Space has to predate computers to be the center of the universe. But if it isn't made of data and websites, what is it? I guess it must be made of thoughts, if it used to be the Qutb network. But in that case how is it different from the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to try and address your questions about &quot;Reality Zones&quot; and &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; because I think it will help a bit with your Edit at the top about Mage saying nothing is true/everything is equally true, because those two things pertain to that specific point.<br /> <br /> I think the specific concept of &quot;Reality Zones&quot; was introduced in M20, but reflected the earlier concepts of Mage regarding the mutability of Truth and its relation to Consensus. The idea of Reality Zones is that, if what is True and the Laws of Reality are determined by Belief, then what rules are actually in play are determined by the local Consensus. For the purpose of game rules, Reality Zones mostly refer to what types of True Magic might be seen as Vulgar versus Coincidental, IIRC. For example, imagine an isolated Fundamentalist Christian community that strongly believes in things like miracles, angels, etc. A Christian Mage with a Christian Focus (methodology/theory for casting magic) could perhaps perform blatantly supernatural acts in public and still be able to treat it as Coincidental rather than Vulgar, because the dominant Consensus in the area allows for it. Conversely, Technocratic tech and abilities might be hindered by Paradox in ways not normally expected if the local Consensus regards it as impossible, or blasphemous. It's a term for the way that Consensual Reality might apply to specific areas.<br /> <br /> To contrast, &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; are rules that are presumably independent of Consensual Reality, to a significant extent at least. There are (perhaps) some things which are True no matter how much Mages or the Consensus might wish otherwise. In usual Mage fashion, actual Earthly Foundations are never discussed AFAIK, they're just a theoretical extrapolation of the belief that SOME PART of Reality has to be independent from the whims of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> PS To actually respond to the OP: as some comments above might indicate, I'm pretty open to the idea that truly immutable Earthly Foundations don't even exist on Earth, so the idea that such a thing holds up in the Near/Deep Umbra makes sense to me. When looking at things from a Mage perspective, I already tend to view different Umbral Realms as Reality Zones shaped by their spiritual denizens. I think the Deep Umbra might be a bit more complicated though, because you have the Deep Umbra that is, to use what I think is the Tychoidian term, &quot;unformatted,&quot; versus Deep Umbra that has been &quot;formatted&quot; but by alien, Lovecraftian, etc., entities. &quot;Unformatted&quot; Deep Umbra could easily be &quot;formatted&quot; to be compatible with a particular Paradigm, whereas the Deep Umbra of Eldritch Abominations might be even more inhospitable to regular Mages but better for Nephandi (associated with the relevant Deep Umbral horror).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 03-19-2021, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T09:57:13-07:00","id":1440729,"title":"","content":"Well there have to be &quot;earthly foundations&quot;, otherwise science would have only ever reinforced the consensus. Science is about searching for what is actually true, and what would actually have been true was whatever people believed was true. Back when everyone believed the world was flat, the world would have actually been flat, and scientific experiments would have only found evidence that the world was, in fact, flat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T10:10:05-07:00","id":1440732,"title":"","content":"And to clarify, Earthly Foundations are explicitly in M20; and they're explicitly <i>not</i> the work of the Technocracy. Arguably, they're something that the Technocracy <i>builds on</i>, which was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a>'s point; but they are not, themselves, a Technocratic invention. <br /> <br /> And getting back to the point of this thread, they arguably don't exist in the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T12:07:27-07:00","id":1440742,"title":"","content":"Let's take this from another angle: what is an Earthly Foundation?<br /> <br /> I don't mean list off specific examples of possible Earthly Foundations, but rather to determine the actual criteria or nature. If an Earthly Foundation is an eternal metaphysical Truth, where does it come from? To apply it to Dataweaver's idea, why would one part of the Tellurian possess such traits, but others not?<br /> <br /> Rather than viewing the Earthly Foundations as independent Truths, I instead prefer to frame them as a consequence of metaphorical inertia, or accretion. What are regarded as Earthly Foundations are not absolutely immutable, but rather practically so; there is so much &quot;weight&quot; behind those ideas, built up over millennia, that they have a stability that other facets of Reality do not, making them more difficult, or even impossible, for Mages to overcome in &quot;typical&quot; fashion.<br /> <br /> To apply this back to Dataweaver's original point: in this framing, I would probably disagree that (&quot;formatted&quot;) Umbra lacks Earthly Foundations, but rather that the Earthly Foundations of those Realms are fundamentally different from those on Earth. Part of where this theory definitely starts to tread on established Mage lore is that it requires entities other than humans to have some kind of effect on/contribution to the Consensus. But then, I tend to enjoy kicking all of the gamelines in some of their assumptions, and undermining the Humanity-As-Exceptional component seems like the best spot to smack Mage egotism in the 'nads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T12:51:38-07:00","id":1440746,"title":"","content":"Let me counter with this: historical inertia is certainly one possible explanation for Earthly Foundations (though it doesn't explain how the whole thing for started). Another possible explanation is that they exist because a powerful spiritual entity (such as God or Gaia) wants them to. A third possible explanation is that they're exactly what they're called: the foundations of Earthly reality, the natural \u201cshape\u201d that's inherent in the fabric of the Tapestry. Any of these might be true. The end result is the same: if there's a way to change them, it takes a lot more than it takes to change a Reality Zone. And that's saying something. In theory, they might be mutable; in practice, they rarely are: the most you can do is to temporarily override them with your Magick. <br /> <br /> I can see Realms in the Umbra having something equivalent to Earthly Foundations: rules of the Realm that hold true no matter what the denizens might happen to believe. But I think it's just as likely that in the various Umbral Realms, you're not going to find any where the locals' beliefs are at odds with the local reality. That's what it would mean to not have anything like Earthly Foundations. They would still have a reality Zone that defines what is Coincidental and what is Vulgar, but there wouldn't be anything pertaining to that Realm that couldn't be changed through the mechanisms involved in changing a Reality Zone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T13:09:05-07:00","id":1440748,"title":"","content":"And to address one of the concerns raised by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar896_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"896\" data-vbnamecard=\"896\">Erinys</a> : Mages don't know everything. Neither does anyone else. What that means is that there are hard and fast rules about how things work in a practical sense, but there are always multiple possible explanations as to why they work that way. See my recent post about the nature of Earthly foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T15:21:28-07:00","id":1440757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440742#post1440742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's take this from another angle: what is an Earthly Foundation?<br /> <br /> I don't mean list off specific examples of possible Earthly Foundations, but rather to determine the actual criteria or nature. If an Earthly Foundation is an eternal metaphysical Truth, where does it come from? To apply it to Dataweaver's idea, why would one part of the Tellurian possess such traits, but others not?<br /> <br /> Rather than viewing the Earthly Foundations as independent Truths, I instead prefer to frame them as a consequence of metaphorical inertia, or accretion. What are regarded as Earthly Foundations are not absolutely immutable, but rather practically so; there is so much &quot;weight&quot; behind those ideas, built up over millennia, that they have a stability that other facets of Reality do not, making them more difficult, or even impossible, for Mages to overcome in &quot;typical&quot; fashion.<br /> <br /> To apply this back to Dataweaver's original point: in this framing, I would probably disagree that (&quot;formatted&quot;) Umbra lacks Earthly Foundations, but rather that the Earthly Foundations of those Realms are fundamentally different from those on Earth. Part of where this theory definitely starts to tread on established Mage lore is that it requires entities other than humans to have some kind of effect on/contribution to the Consensus. But then, I tend to enjoy kicking all of the gamelines in some of their assumptions, and undermining the Humanity-As-Exceptional component seems like the best spot to smack Mage egotism in the 'nads.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't work, because if it were true, we'd all still be living under the Dreamspeaker paradigm, or whatever preceded it. Far from supplanting it, science would just reinforce that paradigm, as scientific studies would only find evidence that it was true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:04:30-07:00","id":1440766,"title":"","content":"Well... <i>science</i> can't advance without the Earthly foundations, for the reasons you state. But magic is another story. Magic isn't about finding evidence that things aren't what they seem and then expanding on that; magic, especially in mage, is about declaring that I want things to be different than they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:31:34-07:00","id":1440772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440766#post1440766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... <i>science</i> can't advance without the Earthly foundations, for the reasons you state..</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it can advance, but it's advancing would be in the context of reinforcing and extrapolating on whatever the first paradigm to ever exist was. Which is more or less the Dreamspeaker paradigm. Everything we can do now and more science would eventually give us, but it would be in the sense of supplicate this spirit this way, and supplicate that spirit that way, Supplicating the spirits would be a scientific fact, and all invention would be more efficient and effective methods of supplicating the spirits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T17:05:33-07:00","id":1440781,"title":"","content":"\u2026unless and until the first witch decides that herbs have medicinal properties distinct from whatever spirits may or may not inhabit them, and uses her enlightened will to make it so. Or until the first ascetic decides that everything has a life force that can be channeled through meditation, and uses mind over matter to make it so. Or until the first devotee decides that God spoke to her and have her a mission. Or until the first proto-Hermetic decides that symbols have power in and of themselves, and Wills it to be true. Just to give a few examples. <br /> <br /> And yes, scientists would latch onto each of these, refine them, and produce technologies out of them that resemble highly efficient versions of the originals. What you <i>don't</i> get without Earthly Foundations is cogs and gears, electricity, nuclear physics, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-10-2022, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T17:44:55-07:00","id":1440785,"title":"","content":"Another reality zone type might be caused by powerful spirits that want human inhabitants of their area/realm. Picture a group of Umbrood that want human inhabitants of their planet/world because they want cultural features to their world. When the reality storm hits they offer standed mages, horizon zone dwellers, and space colonists, a home and survival. There are rules, but mages can make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T18:18:15-07:00","id":1440789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440785#post1440785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reality zone type might be caused by powerful spirits that want human inhabitants of their area/realm. Picture a group of Umbrood that want human inhabitants of their planet/world because they want cultural features to their world. When the reality storm hits they offer standed mages, horizon zone dwellers, and space colonists, a home and survival. There are rules, but mages can make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Oh hey, Changeling: the Lost. Fancy seeing you invited to this party!!!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T20:35:02-07:00","id":1440797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440789#post1440789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>&amp;quot;Oh hey, Changeling: the Lost. Fancy seeing you invited to this party!!!&amp;quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I picture something less obviously cruel. And less kidnapping more exploiting the desperate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T21:04:46-07:00","id":1440804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440746#post1440746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me counter with this: historical inertia is certainly one possible explanation for Earthly Foundations (though it doesn't explain how the whole thing for started). Another possible explanation is that they exist because a powerful spiritual entity (such as God or Gaia) wants them to. A third possible explanation is that they're exactly what they're called: the foundations of Earthly reality, the natural \u201cshape\u201d that's inherent in the fabric of the Tapestry. Any of these might be true. The end result is the same: if there's a way to change them, it takes a lot more than it takes to change a Reality Zone. And that's saying something. In theory, they might be mutable; in practice, they rarely are: the most you can do is to temporarily override them with your Magick.<br /> <br /> I can see Realms in the Umbra having something equivalent to Earthly Foundations: rules of the Realm that hold true no matter what the denizens might happen to believe. But I think it's just as likely that in the various Umbral Realms, you're not going to find any where the locals' beliefs are at odds with the local reality. That's what it would mean to not have anything like Earthly Foundations. They would still have a reality Zone that defines what is Coincidental and what is Vulgar, but there wouldn't be anything pertaining to that Realm that couldn't be changed through the mechanisms involved in changing a Reality Zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct that I am just positing one hypothetical explanation that will likely have very little impact on the individual actions of a single Mage in the context of a chronicle. It's more a big-cosmological-consideration, but it does have implications on the metaphysics of things like Reality Zones. I think the discussion of what Earthly Foundations are supposed to be is relevant to a discussion of whether or not they are present in the Umbra. It's all well and good to say &quot;who knows&quot; from an IC perspective, but the OOC Storyteller deciding whether or not the Umbra has Earthly Foundations, or an equivalent, should probably have an idea of what they mean when they say that.<br /> <br /> And yes, you do need to go back and define the history that created the situation if you do want to go with &quot;historical inertia&quot; like I do, if you want to avoid an infinite regress. Aside from it still being very WIP, I felt the specific point about the possible nature Earthly Foundations was more relevant than my entire pet-theory for the History of the Big World of Darkness :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T11:30:09-07:00","id":1440841,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is that the entirety of the Otherworlds were once all just one Reality Zone, split apart into its various components for some unknown reason and forces. Many of the rules from the original survive in the separate regions, as they were once the same. Over time, some of the rules in some parts changed, others did not. In fact, who is to say that physical reality is even the center of everything. It could just be another level, and something else is the true center, such as Midgard/Alder Bore/etc. It is possible that there is way to connect every part of the WOD's Otherworlds into something more coherent. I've been working on something of late to that effect. Every one of my six sections of Reality, with a separate central locale, share a few basic rules, with individual realms either adding or subtracting rules when necessary. Beings of enough power could change this set-up as needed. This includes Mages at times. Just because something seems to be a rule at a certain time, doesn't mean it will stay that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T05:51:30-07:00","id":1440934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440729#post1440729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there have to be &quot;earthly foundations&quot;, otherwise science would have only ever reinforced the consensus. Science is about searching for what is actually true, and what would actually have been true was whatever people believed was true. Back when everyone believed the world was flat, the world would have actually been flat, and scientific experiments would have only found evidence that the world was, in fact, flat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how I run things: back when everyone believed the world was flat (which was several thousand years ago) the world was flat. At least the parts of it coherent enough to have a shape were flat. It makes surprisingly little difference to history in Mage. <br /> <br /> I also have some objection to your description of science, especially as it pertains to Mage. Science isn't clean, even in our world. There are still pet theories that are given more leeway than other, less accepted ones. Scientists still make claims they can't actually back up. Galileo, for instance, made a famously bad claim that comets were atmospheric effects, prompting the Jesuits to comment that if he thought that he must have never looked at one through a telescope. As it turns out, he hadn't*.<br /> <br /> *The entire story between Galileo and the Church isn't a simple science vs religion thing as people make it out to be. It is a soap opera of personality clashes, stubbornness, and mathematics.<br /> <br /> The point here is that scientists are not prevented from working with incomplete or inconsistent information. There's nothing about the world of Mage that would stop them from trying to bring forward theories that didn't fully match the data and changing the world as they did so. While I do agree that some things like gravity and inertia (call them Earthly Foundations if you like) need to be more robust than others, they do not need to be unchanging or unchangeable. Indeed, changing paradigms make more sense if these things are only consistent in the broad strokes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T09:52:27-07:00","id":1440951,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Earthly Foundations aren't unchangeable; a mage changes things whenever she performs a work of Magick that is Vulgar according to the Earthly Foundations. <br /> <br /> As for whether they're unchangeable in the long run: I tend to think that they are, and that this is what the Technocracy does whenever it successfully incorporates one of its innovations so thoroughly into the fabric of reality that it no longer even counts as Magick anymore; not even Coincidental Magick. But that's a slow and arduous process, even moreso than changing a Reality Zone; and there's more involved than <i>just</i> altering the Consensus. At the <i>very least</i>, you need to <i>maintain</i> the Consensus in a state that's at odds with the underlying Earthly Foundations, for long enough that the latter adjusts to match the former. That's easier to do when your making small, incremental changes, which is why the Technocracy has a Timetable: said Timetable is their estimate as to how quickly they can get their improvements incorporated into the Earthly Foundations so that they're not available <i>just</i> to Enlightened Scientists and Extraordinary Citizens, but to <i>everyone</i>. <br /> <br /> Going back to my original premise: some good points have been made here, and I'm tweaking my thesis. There are indeed Umbral versions of the Earthly Foundations. But there's a different set of Umbral Foundations for each Umbra: the Dark Umbra has one set; the Middle Umbra has another set; the Astral Umbra has a third set; and Etherspace has a fourth set. I still say that the Deep Umbra is characterized by its lack of Umbral Foundations. Umbral Realms are the Reality Zones of the Umbrae; and they can exist anywhere, including the Deep Umbra (see the Realms of the eldtrich abominations that reside out there). But even in so-called \u201cunformatted Umbra\u201d, the are a handful of rules that exist that are characteristic of the Umbral \u201clayer\u201d (Dark, Middle, Astral, or Ether) such as who gets to hang around with minimal risk of Disembodiment; and <i>those</i> are the Umbral Foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T10:01:31-07:00","id":1440952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440934#post1440934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(call them Earthly Foundations if you like)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I call them Earthly Foundations because M20 calls them Earthly Foundations. And the manuscript for Victorian Mage, which makes a bigger deal about how Reality Zones change than M20 does, talks about how if a Territory (its term for Reality Zone) gets purged of all residents, then eventually it reverts to the Earthly Foundations. Ultimately, that's what they are: what Reality is like <i>without</i> the Consensus altering it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T11:40:45-07:00","id":1440955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440952#post1440952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I call them Earthly Foundations because M20 calls them Earthly Foundations. And the manuscript for Victorian Mage, which makes a bigger deal about how Reality Zones change than M20 does, talks about how if a Territory (its term for Reality Zone) gets purged of all residents, then eventually it reverts to the Earthly Foundations. Ultimately, that's what they are: what Reality is like <i>without</i> the Consensus altering it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I added the parentheses because I was using the idea of a gravity and inertia that were more robust than some other things but not necessarily written in stone. While I certainly think that is a reasonable description of Earthly Foundations, many people do not and I wasn't going to force the issue.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T11:46:26-07:00","id":1440956,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Ultimately, the defining feature of an Earthly Foundation is that something can be Vulgar (or Coincidental, for that matter) even when the Consensus says otherwise. Anything further, such as where they come from or whether they can be changed (and if so, how), is speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-22-2021, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T12:47:45-07:00","id":1441108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: See, my difficulty with Mage consensus cosmology is that it seems to say nothing is true, or everything is equally true. Then we can't say anything definitive about anything. But yet there have to be definite game rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage cosmology isn't about everything being equally true or false. It's more about truth being non-binary, and more up for grabs. As has been pointed out by others, there are Earthly Foundations which resist being redefined by the Consensus, meaning that the Consensus isn't always right \u2014 which is a good thing, because the Consensus has had some pretty dumb ideas in it at times. <br /> <br /> All that said, it <i>is</i> harder to say anything definitive in Mage; that's kind of the point: to a large extent, Reality is what you make of it. There are also some meta-rules, such as the game systems for working Magick; but what these <i>mean</i> it's something open to interpretation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit worlds collectively are a heck of a lot larger and deeper than the material worlds, so it's hard to argue that the material world is more fundamental. Being a place of spirit-less matter, the material world is the odd duck out. Or the material world and the Shade Realm of Matter. Assuming the former isn't somewhere inside the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 introduced the notion of Reality Zones, which means that there isn't a single, global Consensus; instead, there are a lot of local ones. This means that it doesn't matter how vast something is, for the most part; the residents in New York City have no say in the Reality Zones in upper New York State, and vice versa. And that's with New York city's population being much larger than those of the upper New York State zones, individually and possibly even collectively. So the fact that the Umbra is far larger than Earth doesn't give them dominance in the reality shaping game.<br /> <br /> On top of that, there's some question as to whether or not spirits contribute to the Consensus at all. On Earth, animals don't; only creatures with Avatars do. That is, humans. And for the most part, it's agreed that spirits don't have Avatars. There might be a few exceptions, such as the fabled Pure Ones; and those entities at the very top of the spiritual hierarchy probably do have the ability to shape reality. Yes, this includes the Triat. I'll get back to this a bit further down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The science+technology = Bad concept wasn't a good design choice for either game, really. I have a friend who loves the CofD but can't stand the cWoD because of it, and I can't really blame her.</div> </div> </div> </div> Neither can I, which is why I've put so much effort into countering that narrative. It is, for example, the main reason why I latched on to the Navalon craft: as I envision them, they let you decouple the Technocracy's Science from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Technocracy are also all about control, about limiting possibilities and options, about censoring knowledge as a weapon to remove things from reality, and about explaining everything in reductionistic ways that eliminate spirituality, souls, intuition, and lots of other details that they know do actually exist. Those goals are also Stasis. (In Werewolf terms, Stasis and the Weaver would be the same thing. By definition, nothing but the Almighty Creator can be bigger than the Weaver because it's inherently 1/3 of all reality.) If Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy are each 1/3 of reality in Mage, then the same is true: you can't have something bigger than Stasis, except for God/the One.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you say, Werewolf's position is that Stasis and the Weaver are one and the same. By contrast, Mage takes the position that the map is not the terrain. The spirit of a tree is not the tree. And the spirit of Stasis, the Weaver, is not Stasis. <br /> <br /> Also, arguments for and against the existence of the Christian God apply equally well to the Triat: how do we know that they exist? Has anyone met them personally (and can we trust those who claim to have), or have they only interacted with spirits that claim to serve them? Sure, there's such a thing as Wyrm taint; but that doesn't mean that there's an overall self-aware entity responsible for it. Yes, werewolves believe it to be so; but that doesn't automatically make it so. Not in a Mage game, at least. In fact, M20 specifically leaves it up to the Storyteller to decide what's at the top of the spiritual hierarchy.<br /> <br /> And even if the Weaver does exist, that doesn't mean that the Technocracy serves it. It may just be that they have goals that overlap to an extent. Emphasis on \u201cto an extent\u201d: just because the Weaver has a particular goal, it doesn't automatically follow that the Technocracy does as well. And there <i>are</i> differences: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And how can the things Technocrats tell the 'Masses' not be lies? They say magic is impossible, that &quot;reality deviants&quot; and spirits don't exist, but they know all three are real and do exist. They insist there is no spirit world, but they know it exists and how to enter it. They censor scientific discoveries that they don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, to an extent. And the organization as a whole is problematic. But two things: first, why should the Storyteller nerf Science because Technocrats are jerks? <br /> <br /> And the Union doesn't do what it does because it wants to crush the human soul. Technocrats are motivated by a desire to help and protect the Masses. The things that they oppose, they don't oppose because they don't believe in them; they opposed them because they think that they're dangerous. Even the control that they seek isn't a goal in and of itself; it's a means to an end. They don't trust Sleepers to take care of themselves, and they think that they know better. Technocracy Reloaded goes so far as to say that they now consider the Masses to be the greatest danger that the Masses face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't saying the Technocrats created the Gauntlet or Shroud, of course. They appear to be making the Gauntlet thicker, but both barriers would have been created in prehistoric times, like the Stone Age or even earlier. Wraith seems to say the Shroud was created by the fear of death. Werewolf says the Gauntlet was created by the Weaver. In a unified WoD, <b>or</b> in Mage, humans couldn't know because they have no recorded history (oral or written) old enough to tell them anything about that time period. No Mage craft or Tradition is that old, so how would they know what happened then? Let alone claiming to know how the universe was created - humans didn't exist then so how would they know? Some spirits could know, but most mages don't talk to spirits, and some spirits could be lying. And if a spirit says &quot;this god created XYZ&quot; to an atheist mage, the mage'll just ignore what it said.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. and the same holds true of werewolves, vampires, wraiths, changelings, and every other denizen of the World of Darkness. They all have their beliefs about the origins of the universe, but none have any way to verify. (Unless, of course, a group of mages perform a Time-based great work and collect enough successes to witness the creation of the universe). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned Earthly Foundations several times. Is this some term from the Technocratic paradigm, or an OOC game term? I have the same question about &quot;Reality Zone&quot;, too.</div> </div> </div> </div> both are OOC terms. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree, at least not in an absolute sense. Maybe in Mage that is the case, but in terms of worldbuilding a plausible fantasy setting it isn't necessarily true. Some magic may require a higher level spell but that isn't the same as being absolutely impossible to do. It's possible to invent an internally-consistent fantasy magic system in which absolutely anything can be accomplished.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's fine; I didn't state it as an absolute, just a tendency: to truly have a system that can do literally anything requires a lot of work, both in creating it and in maintaining it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440612#post1440612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for clearing up my misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adept paradigm is one I've never been able to understand. The Virtual Space has to predate computers to be the center of the universe. But if it isn't made of data and websites, what is it? I guess it must be made of thoughts, if it used to be the Qutb network. But in that case how is it different from the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's made of information, which I would say is to thoughts as Matter is to Life. How it differs from the Astral Umbra is a good question; but it <i>does</i> differ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-26-2021, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T17:28:06-07:00","id":1441164,"title":"","content":"Yeah or to lay it out:<br /> <br /> Trying to map Werewolf's Triat to Mage's cosmology just...doesn't really hold up. It suggests a rigidity to the various mage organizations that just doesn't work, or isn't internally consistent when you see the lore about how these groups operate.<br /> <br /> Even breaking down the Union, if we tried to map them out to Essences it would be more like this: <br /> <br /> NWO: Pattern/Primordial<br /> Syndicate: Pattern/Dynamic<br /> Iteration X: Dynamic<br /> Progenitors: Dynamic<br /> Void Engineers: Questing/Primordial<br /> <br /> (nvm that saying the garou themselves are agents of the Wyld ...just doesn't really work either, but that's beyond the scope of a Mage thread)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441108#post1441108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't trust Sleepers to take care of themselves, and they think that they know better. Technocracy Reloaded goes so far as to say that they now consider the Masses to be the greatest danger that the Masses face.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here? THIS is the true personal horror that's unique to Mage and is far more front and center then Vampire's or Werewolf's brand of personal horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T18:04:57-07:00","id":1441171,"title":"","content":"Yeah; trying to equate Mage factions to the Triat makes about as much sense as saying, e.g., that the Camarilla corresponds to the Weaver, the Anarchs correspond to the Wyld, and the Sabbat corresponds to the Wyrm. There might have been something to it in the first edition of Mage; but that ship has long since sailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T21:26:44-07:00","id":1441192,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's always been something off about the idea that the science guys were about stasis, and a group literally named the &quot;Traditions&quot; was about dynamism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T21:40:17-07:00","id":1441193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441192#post1441192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's always been something off about the idea that the science guys were about stasis, and a group literally named the &quot;Traditions&quot; was about dynamism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <br /> A lot of the Traditions and Crafts want to make things back the way they were, aka &quot;things were better in the good old days&quot;...which technically fulfills the definition of &quot;conservative&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T04:52:09-07:00","id":1441230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441192#post1441192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's always been something off about the idea that the science guys were about stasis, and a group literally named the &quot;Traditions&quot; was about dynamism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is indeed ironic that the science faction is more static than the traditional faction, but the Technocracy's static tendencies have little to do with their hard sciences. The scientific side of the Technocracy, the timetable and the rollout of new technologies are among their more dynamic elements. <br /> <br /> That said, the world the Technocracy fights for is one with a single (or multiple very closely related) world view(s). That is static, in goal if not in method. This world view may grow over time, but in a methodical predictable way. Stasis. <br /> <br /> But I wouldn't say it is off because most mages can't help but be Dynamic. Whatever their affiliation or Avatar type, they still fight for a world that doesn't yet exist. Outside of the theoretical completely Static mage, all of them are trying to change the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T09:27:53-07:00","id":1441261,"title":"","content":"\u2026with the arguable exception of the Negation Men, yes. (And that's another thing that Mage does: everything has an exception.)<br /> <br /> Also notice that there are four Essences in mage, not three. Dynamic Essence has a lot in common with Dynamism and the Wyld; the Pattern Essence has some overlap with Stasis and the Weaver, though less than the overlap between Dynamic and Dynamism. And after that, there really isn't much of a connection: MRev attempted to associate the Primordial Essence with Entropy and the Wyrm; but that was more of a \u201cleast bad fit\u201d than anything else. And the Questing Essence simply has no counterpart in the Triat: MRev tried to address that by calling it a balance between the other three; but it just isn't: the \u201cbalance between Essences\u201d, of such a thing exists, would be the mysterious Infinite Essence, which is talked about in much the same way that the Tenth Sphere is: something aspirational, but not something that anyone has ever seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T09:50:47-07:00","id":1441264,"title":"","content":"Anyway, the main point I was going for before I got sidetracked was that Stasis could use some revision in the context of Mage: as Ramnesis pointed out, all mages are inherently \u201cdynamic\u201d, in the sense that they're looking to change the world. If we're going to give a single word for what the Technocracy is trying to do, I'd prefer Pattern to Stasis: the latter has the connotation of being opposed to change, whereas the former has the connotation of preferring structure. <br /> <br /> And in that regard, I tend to view the Timetable as a <i>conservative</i> thing: not in the Stasis sense of resistance to change, but in the more Pattern sense of being careful not to screw anything up as you advance: building out from the existing structure and making sure that what you add doesn't have unintended consequences that will screw up what you already have. In <i>that</i> sense, I could see calling the Technocracy \u201cconservative\u201d. In short, I see it as having <i>everything</i> to do with their science, while having very little too do with their policies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-24-2021, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T07:47:57-07:00","id":1441373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't trust Sleepers to take care of themselves, and they think that they know better. Technocracy Reloaded goes so far as to say that they now consider the Masses to be the greatest danger that the Masses face.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441164#post1441164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This right here? THIS is the true personal horror that's unique to Mage and is far more front and center then Vampire's or Werewolf's brand of personal horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS ... being that mages think they know better, not &quot;<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O7QE6w4JF-U&amp;ab_channel=BlackFoxx\" target=\"_blank\">humans</a>&quot; - Well, <i>it kinda IS Man </i>but in the guise of mages, not so much the nameless masses. One word:<br /> <br /> <b>Hubris</b><br /> <br /> Hubris defines the Mages as much as the Jyhad defines vampires, like the Technocracy believing they're <i>moraly </i> more advanced than the rest of humanity, when it's constantly shown that Awakening doesn't do anything for personal ethics or common sense wisdom, and more often than not fosters a fundamentalist viewpoint about Reality even among mages that <i>should </i>aprove any other focuses, like among the Traditions.<br /> <br /> <i>Trying to win the Ascencion War</i> understood as collapsing the cosmos under one Focus (as in &quot;One World, One Truth, One Reality&quot; being the lema behind eradicating or neutering beliefs out of fear for unaligned Focuses), hence eliminating a degree of Dynamism, it's a vision of Statism.<br /> <br /> Oviously nothing of this it's going to bring a world like what the Weaver wants because mages are still human and thus even the most static won't likely desire to be frozen in time, but it's still a vision of Statism on a more human scale<br /> <br /> For what it's worth: In the Book of the Weaver it's said that while the Technocracy it's playing along with Weaver's agenda, they're ultimately to be eradicated because all mages warp reality - and the Weaver does not want that. The Weaver <i>could </i>be the force behind Paradox, in that worldview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-25-2021, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T03:17:25-07:00","id":1441480,"title":"","content":"It's even more ironic to associate the Technocracy with stasis, given that they are the group that most commony *changes* and adjusts the world more than any other. Heck, they overhauled the world at large in passing centuries.<br /> Just because they don't like the changes *others* have in mind does not mean that they, themselves, are static; Not at all. Anything else is a very, VERY 1st-edition view of the Union. Even order requires change and adjustment ever so often.<br /> <br /> As M20 points out no Mage is static. They always have the drive to advance and learn and seek. Even those among the Union.<br /> Their nature and essence might be one of stability, patterns and logic, but no Mage is associated with literal stasis. The exception *might* be the Negation Men type of Marauders as they are essentially anti-Marauders in a way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-26-2021, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T20:25:25-07:00","id":1441594,"title":"","content":"I have had some really bad days and trouble putting my thoughts in words. I can\u2019t keep up with how fast everyone else posts. This might come across angry but I am not angry, just having a really really bad day at work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441108#post1441108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage cosmology isn't about everything being equally true or false. It's more about truth being non-binary, and more up for grabs. As has been pointed out by others, there are Earthly Foundations which resist being redefined by the Consensus, meaning that the Consensus isn't always right \u2014 which is a good thing, because the Consensus has had some pretty dumb ideas in it at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have to table my &quot;Help me grok Mage&quot; thread/derail until [the construction ends and I can] get some decent sleep. Or until I find time to read M20, <i>ooohhh my god it's like 700 pages long.</i><br /> <br /> But, uh, yeah there have to be things that don't change. Lots of big things. Otherwise, millennia before empires and evangelical religions and colonialism and the Order of Reason and globalism started assimilating everyone, the Earth would have... exploded into separate pieces. Not just separate Umbral Realms, I mean the Earth would be a bunch of city-sized pocket universes unconnected to each other. In fact there has to be something holding together Reality Zones with utterly incompatible cosmology and theology. Because the 6000-year-old sin-dirtied Fallen world created by an omniscient transcendent God is not remotely compatible with the billions-of-years-old atheist world of mechanistic particles, or the Pagan world that's is the soul of a living immanent Divinity where every single patch of earth is sacred ground. Those aren't even separate Umbras, they're separate <i>genres</i>.<br /> <br /> I can comprehend not knowing what is True, but where the most fundamental foundations of the cosmos change by the city block, or by the decade? Nope does not compute. Maybe I'm too much the literal thinker. I'm a big Planescape fan, but this is .... blkdsahuhsdnfnjksh<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441108#post1441108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 introduced the notion of Reality Zones, which means that there isn't a single, global Consensus; instead, there are a lot of local ones. This means that it doesn't matter how vast something is, for the most part; the residence in New York City have no say in the Reality Zones in upper New York State, and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed my point. For every physical, material, spirit-less world, there are a whole bunch of matter-less spirit worlds not to mention there's that whole information Hypersphere. It's pretty clear that the vast majority of the cosmos(es) is (are) spiritual or mental, not material. A spirit-less, fae-less world made out of particles is the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441108#post1441108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you say, Werewolf's position is that Stasis and the Weaver are one and the same. By contrast, Mage takes the position that the map is not the terrain. The spirit of a tree is not the tree. And the spirit of Stasis, the Weaver, is not Stasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Weaver is not the \u201cspirit of\u201d Stasis. The Weaver isn\u2019t a \u201cspirit <b>of</b>\u201d anything in Werewolf. It is an impersonal, non-material force of nature which shapeshifters personify in their sacred myths. The way it\u2019s personified in their stories just doesn\u2019t matter at a cosmic level. It\u2019s not literally a spider, it just <i>has</i> spiders. If you have a hangup with it being personified, just ignore that .<br /> <br /> There are 3 problems causing confusion here about Stasis/Weaver.<br /> <br /> #1 Is that every Werewolf book, and all the shapeshifters, personify the Triat. Everything they see has an intelligent spirit, and they feel the love of Gaia in their souls. So they assume that huge cosmic forces are people too. They depict them having arguments, going insane, suffering pain, etc. <b>But,</b> there\u2019s no proof that the Triat are people in any such way (the Urge-Wyrms seem to suggest it, but aren\u2019t proof). Nobody talks directly to them. Queen Ananasa, who apparently interacted directly with them, describes them in personified terms to her Ananasi children, but who knows if that\u2019s metaphor, or dumbing down something transcendent, or just lies. And note that they\u2019re rarely or never called \u2018spirits\u2019. They transcend spirits the way Oracles transcend dogs. They are almost certainly far too vast to be called people, let alone specifically spirits.<br /> <br /> If you can look past how the shapeshifters reflexively personify everything IC, it\u2019s clear the writers intended the Triat and Metaphysic Trinity to be the same. They are three vast cosmic forces that move the Tellurian: creation/change, preservation/stability/stasis, and destruction/entropy. God only knows if they\u2019re intelligent people or mindless energy fields or neither or both or blue. The cosmos sure seems to be out of \u201cbalance\u201d but nobody entirely understands what that truly means.<br /> <br /> And on the other hand, I doubt there is OOC proof in Mage that the Metaphysical Trinity absolutely are not, have never been, cannot possibly be, sapient or sentient in any way at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> #2 Problem is that the writers unwisely tied all technological invention to Stasis. Perhaps this was supposed to be a post-modern Statement about industrial \u2018progress\u2019, but it sends the wrong message and makes no sense. Changeling handles this much better. Lots of technological inventions are more Dynamic or Entropic than Static.<br /> <br /> <br /> #3 Problem is that Stasis is poorly named. The Changeling name is more fitting: Banality. Or call it Reductionism. That drive to reduce everything to physics and chemistry, to eliminate all notions of the spiritual, the sacred, the religious, the life-forces of beings, the <i>meaning</i> of things and events. To discover and name and catalogue and control <i>everything</i>, to end mystery and chaos and the unknown. I compiled a list of examples but I don't want to derail another thread.<br /> <br /> The Metaphysic Trinity encompass the entire cosmos and <i>every</i> possible action and concept with only 3 forces. Everything not exquisitely balanced is tilted towards one or two of them somehow. And probably, Banality/Stasis is to healthy Preservation what Nephandic perversity is to normal healthy Destruction/Entropy/Death, and Marauder batshit insanity is to healthy Dynamism.<br /> <br /> OOCly, in 1E the Marauders, Technocrats, and Nephandi seem to be antagonists representing insane extremes of the Trinity. Then they [realized science=bad was stupid and] made the Technocrats playable, and finally made the crazy Stasis-freaks into Threat Null instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441108#post1441108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. and the same holds true of werewolves, vampires, wraiths, changelings, and every other denizen of the World of Darkness. They all have their beliefs about the origins of the universe, but none have any way to verify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which is why you shouldn't take it literally when they call the Weaver a Spider. Or a spirit.<br /> <br /> (I was originally talking about having records of events in the most recent Ice Age, which is a different story from anyone knowing how the universe was created or what the Wyrm's favorite apterif is.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441108#post1441108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's made of information, which I would say is to thoughts as Matter is to Life. How it differs from the Astral Umbra is a good question; but it <i>does</i> differ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okaayy... still not comprehending. Are you able to expand on this? Maybe in another thread if you prefer? Or refer to a page # in M20 that would help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-26-2021, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T05:09:58-07:00","id":1441629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had some really bad days and trouble putting my thoughts in words. I can\u2019t keep up with how fast everyone else posts. This might come across angry but I am not angry, just having a really really bad day at work.</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, you have my sympathy. I've also been going through a rough time recently. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have to table my &amp;quot;Help me grok Mage&amp;quot; thread/derail until [the construction ends and I can] get some decent sleep. Or until I find time to read M20, <i>ooohhh my god it's like 700 pages long.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah; I get that, too. One thing I really hope that they do when M5 comes out eventually is to go with a <i>much</i> smaller core book, and to introduce Mage's themes and ideas a bit at a time instead of dumping everything on the reader all at once. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can comprehend not knowing what is True, but where the most fundamental foundations of the cosmos change by the city block, or by the decade? Nope does not compute. Maybe I'm too much the literal thinker. I'm a big Planescape fan, but this is .... blkdsahuhsdnfnjksh</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm <i>still</i> with you. All that stuff you just said about there needing to be some things that don't change? That's what Earthly Foundations are all about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed my point. For every physical, material, spirit-less world, there are a whole bunch of matter-less spirit worlds not to mention there's that whole information Hypersphere. It's pretty clear that the vast majority of the cosmos(es) is (are) spiritual or mental, not material. A spirit-less, fae-less world made out of particles is the exception, not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is where we start to disagree \u2014 though even here, I'm willing to agree that the non-material parts of reality are far more vast than the material parts. Where I disagree with you is whether or not that <i>matters</i>. What I was trying to say is that the material world doesn't define what the Umbra is like, but the Umbra doesn't define what the material world is like either. It isn't a reality-wide majority rule system; where the nature of reality is open to influence by beliefs, it's primarily a local thing: the Earthly Foundations establish some basic ground rules for how things work; but beyond that, reality is defined on the local level. The vast expanses of the Umbra are too separated from the material world to partake in defining it. Earth is defined by its Earthly Foundations and by the Reality Zones created by the beliefs of those residents of Earth who have Avatars; the Umbrae are defined by their counterparts to the Earthly Foundations. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Weaver is not the \u201cspirit of\u201d Stasis. The Weaver isn\u2019t a \u201cspirit <b>of</b>\u201d anything in Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will defer to you in terms of what Werewolf says. I've never been a fan of the game; and while I'm not ignorant of it, not do I have the sort of deep knowledge of it that I have of Mage. But by the same token, that's Werewolf; it isn't Mage. In mage, there's an \u201cUmbral Powers Hierarchy\u201d, with Greater Spirit Entities at the top, starting with \u201cEssential Divinity\u201d (e.g., God/Goddess/the Great Spirit/the One), Godheads/Celestines/God-Avatars (e.g., Zeus, Inanna, Jesus, Krishna, Satan, Grandfather, the Wyrm, Maiden/Mother/Crow, etc.), and so on. Heck, even Werewolf describes the Triat as being at the top of the hierarchy of spirits. You describe the Weaver as a personification of a cosmic force: it is in that sense that I mean that it's the spirit of Stasis. If you prefer, I'll call it the personification of Stasis; it doesn't change my point: the personification of a thing is not the thing itself. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an impersonal, non-material force of nature which shapeshifters personify in their sacred myths. The way it\u2019s personified in their stories just doesn\u2019t matter at a cosmic level. It\u2019s not literally a spider, it just <i>has</i> spiders. If you have a hangup with it being personified, just ignore that .<br /> <br /> There are 3 problems causing confusion here about Stasis/Weaver.<br /> <br /> #1 Is that every Werewolf book, and all the shapeshifters, personify the Triat. Everything they see has an intelligent spirit, and they feel the love of Gaia in their souls. So they assume that huge cosmic forces are people too. They depict them having arguments, going insane, suffering pain, etc. <b>But,</b> there\u2019s no proof that the Triat are people in any such way (the Urge-Wyrms seem to suggest it, but aren\u2019t proof). Nobody talks directly to them. Queen Ananasa, who apparently interacted directly with them, describes them in personified terms to her Ananasi children, but who knows if that\u2019s metaphor, or dumbing down something transcendent, or just lies. And note that they\u2019re rarely or never called \u2018spirits\u2019. They transcend spirits the way Oracles transcend dogs. They are almost certainly far too vast to be called people, let alone specifically spirits.<br /> <br /> If you can look past how the shapeshifters reflexively personify everything IC, it\u2019s clear the writers intended the Triat and Metaphysic Trinity to be the same. They are three vast cosmic forces that move the Tellurian: creation/change, preservation/stability/stasis, and destruction/entropy. God only knows if they\u2019re intelligent people or mindless energy fields or neither or both or blue. The cosmos sure seems to be out of \u201cbalance\u201d but nobody entirely understands what that truly means.<br /> <br /> And on the other hand, I doubt there is OOC proof in Mage that the Metaphysical Trinity absolutely are not, have never been, cannot possibly be, sapient or sentient in any way at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Of course there isn't. And while you're right that there's an intentional parallel between the Triat and the Metaphysical Trinity, I have to point out that while the Metaphysical Trinity exists in Mage, it doesn't have nearly the same importance in Mage that the Triat has in Werewolf. It basically only appears in two ways in the game \u2014 both, incidentally, being legacies of the Revised edition: first, as an optional rule called Synergy, which describes how mystical energies can have flavors that are broadly categorized as Static, Dynamic, or Entropic; and second, as the three modes of Quiet: Madness, Denial, and Morbidity. That's pretty much it. <br /> <br /> If particular relevance to this discussion, M20 specifically says that efforts to associate the Technocracy with Stasis are an oversimplification. Likewise, there are Nephandi who \u201cserve the Wyrm\u201d; but to say that the Nephandi, as a whole, serve the Wyrm is a gross oversimplification of the Nephandi. And with all three aspects of the Metaphysical Trinity appearing as types of Quiet, the idea that the Marauders are inherently of the Wyld is also suspect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2 Problem is that the writers unwisely tied all technological invention to Stasis. Perhaps this was supposed to be a post-modern Statement about industrial \u2018progress\u2019, but it sends the wrong message and makes no sense. Changeling handles this much better. Lots of technological inventions are more Dynamic or Entropic than Static.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; which is part of why Mage has also moved away from the notion of technology being Static \u2014 as well as the notion of the Technocracy being Static. The other part is that the whole Static/Dynamic/Entropic thing, as I mentioned before, just doesn't have the same central role in Mage that it has in Werewolf. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#3 Problem is that Stasis is poorly named. The Changeling name is more fitting: Banality. Or call it Reductionism. That drive to reduce everything to physics and chemistry, to eliminate all notions of the spiritual, the sacred, the religious, the life-forces of beings, the <i>meaning</i> of things and events. To discover and name and catalogue and control <i>everything</i>, to end mystery and chaos and the unknown. I compiled a list of examples but I don't want to derail another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need; I get the concept. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Metaphysic Trinity encompass the entire cosmos and <i>every</i> possible action and concept with only 3 forces. Everything not exquisitely balanced is tilted towards one or two of them somehow. And probably, Banality/Stasis is to healthy Preservation what Nephandic perversity is to normal healthy Destruction/Entropy/Death, and Marauder batshit insanity is to healthy Dynamism.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026except, as I pointed out, Mage doesn't place the same importance on the Metaphysical Trinity that Werewolf places on the Triat. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOCly, in 1E the Marauders, Technocrats, and Nephandi seem to be antagonists representing insane extremes of the Trinity. Then they [realized science=bad was stupid and] made the Technocrats playable, and finally made the crazy Stasis-freaks into Threat Null instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; though even there, I'm not sure that I'd say that Threat Null is Stasis-freaks. As well, Threat Null is an optional element of Mage; moreso than most of the potential antagonists in the game, it may not even exist. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which is why you shouldn't take it literally when they call the Weaver a Spider. Or a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>personification, then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441594#post1441594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okaayy... still not comprehending. Are you able to expand on this? Maybe in another thread if you prefer? Or refer to a page # in M20 that would help?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread has already been well and truly derailed; so no need to move to another thread. <br /> <br /> Computers don't think; but they process information. A book doesn't remember; but it stores information. A camera doesn't perceive anything; but it records information. Mind and information are <i>related</i>; but they're not the same thing. <br /> <br /> My comparison to Matter versus Life is this: information itself just <i>is</i>, and has a quality to it that's inherently inert, like a rock; a mind, by contrast, has more of the quality of something alive: it grows, changes, acts, reacts, and heals when harmed. Mind you, that's not a sharp distinction: plants are a form of Life, despite being basically inert; and a robot is Matter, despite being animate. It doesn't help that the Digital Web is by definition the part of virtual space that would be analogous to how robotics are part of Matter: it deals with \u201canimate information\u201d that bears a resemblance to mental activities without actually <i>being</i> mental activities. <br /> <br /> Another category scheme to consider is the notion of body, mind, and soul. Life is clearly about the body; but the notion of the body can also be generalized to deal with things that are material (Matter) and even some things that aren't material (Forces). Likewise, Mind is about, well, the mind; but the notion of the mind can be generalized to things that are fundamentally about information, but are outside the scope of the mind in the same way that matter and energy are outside the scope of the body. And virtual space is to information and the mind as the material world is to life, matter, and energy. And the distinction between virtual space and the Umbra is similar to the distinction between the mind and the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T11:58:29-07:00","id":1441670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1441629#post1441629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Computers don't think; but they process information. A book doesn't remember; but it stores information. A camera doesn't perceive anything; but it records information. Mind and information are <i>related</i>; but they're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> My comparison to Matter versus Life is this: information itself just <i>is</i>, and has a quality to it that's inherently inert, like a rock; a mind, by contrast, has more of the quality of something alive: it grows, changes, acts, reacts, and heals when harmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one way of seeing it.<br /> <br /> Other way could be to say that information itself just <i>isn't</i>. Information doesn't exist outside a sentient interpretation. Computers don't process information, they process ligth, electricity...It's the mind that processes the meaningless physical outputs into an meaningfull input, something that we call &quot;information&quot;<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Digital Web denizens are made of Forces instead of Ephemera(Spirit), and the landscape too at least in the first book (and wasn't really changed in the second - it's not explicitly mentioned, but neither it's discredited. And it's used in a Rote).<br /> <br /> It's possible that the Digital Web, much like information, actually reacts to what we think it is: Internet it's computers, information it's strongly related to computation in the modern world, so the Zone it's energy(Forces). Maybe Quaf was Mind, or even Secrets, or another Pillar's concept (if we go by DA)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar896_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"896\" data-vbnamecard=\"896\">Erinys</a> Sorry if I'm making this more complex than it needs to be, I'm just mussing.<br /> <br /> In general terms, it's not part of the Umbra (or it is part of the Umbra in the same sense as the Eartly Realm it's). It actually has a Gauntlet, that one can cross with Spirit 3. If you do that, you end in the Cyberrealm (and you can enter from the Cyberrealm to the digi-web, too. That's how Werewolves and some cyber-shamans enter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-27-2021, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T05:47:51-07:00","id":1442029,"title":"","content":"In Mage, if enough people believe or even imagine something, it gains an existence. Sometimes that existence is even something outside of the High Umbra. There are no given mechanics or metaphysics for this, but I could imagine a very interesting game about trying to husband something from the High Umbra into a more material reality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}